#: folio/dpi-h-ra/ch2-dpi-h-reference-architecture-fra/t-2-4.md:7
msgid "Benefits Package Registry for authoritative benefit definitions and machine-readable reference rules, consumed by operational eligibility, pre-authorisation, and claims systems"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/ch2-dpi-h-reference-architecture-fra/p-2-1-2-93db4e.md:1
msgid "Beyond the two layers, there are certain capabilities that are properties of DPI-H as a whole rather than features of any single component, layer, or business service. <a0>Interoperability</a0> is not a component to be built once but a property that should pervade the architecture through shared standards, common data models, and defined exchange patterns. Governance is cross-cutting in the same way: it applies to every component and capability the architecture describes and is treated as an architecture design principle below and elaborated on in the governance sub-chapter."
msgstr ""

