msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/ch2-dpi-h-reference-architecture-fra/p-2-3-bf2ea8.md:2
msgid "Degrade gracefully and guarantee non-digital routes of equivalent standing. The absence of a given foundational layer — continuous connectivity, a mature national identity system, personal digital devices, or particular facility infrastructure — should reduce what is automated rather than lock a setting or population out entirely. Every function on which a right, clinical service, or health entitlement depends must maintain an assisted and non-digital route of equivalent standing (such as paper-bridged, facility-mediated, or community-health-worker-assisted pathways) so that participation, care access, and consent never depend on individual smartphone ownership or any single digital channel."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/ch2-dpi-h-reference-architecture-fra/p-2-3-f7c393.md:1
msgid "Designed this way, the reference architecture is aspirational in direction but pragmatic in entry point – countries can see themselves in it regardless of where they start, and can adopt the components relevant to them without implementing the whole architecture first. The minimum viable foundation for DPI-H provides a clear, bounded starting point from which capabilities are extended over time, and individual components can be piloted, evaluated, and iterated without disrupting the wider architecture."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/ch2-dpi-h-reference-architecture-fra/p-2-4-1-2352fd.md:1
msgid "Each of the seven priority health goals is articulated using the same structure, so that the mapping is consistent and comparable across goals:"
